1
00:00:00,040 --> 00:00:03,320
[Characters, places and incidents
in this production]

2
00:00:03,320 --> 00:00:06,640
[are entirely fictitious.]

3
00:00:06,640 --> 00:00:09,960
[Viewer discretion is advised.]

4
00:00:59,440 --> 00:01:01,360
<i>If you're sleepy, Auntie...</i>

5
00:01:01,360 --> 00:01:02,520
<i>Why don't you go to sleep?</i>

6
00:01:02,520 --> 00:01:04,840
<i>Since when am I your mom's older sister?</i>

7
00:01:06,199 --> 00:01:08,320
<i>You're being awfully cold
to your fiancée, Yai.</i>

8
00:01:08,320 --> 00:01:09,800
<i>Are you still not used to it?</i>

9
00:01:09,800 --> 00:01:11,440
<i>Are you still not over her?</i>

10
00:01:11,440 --> 00:01:13,640
<i>If you're so smart, then don't upset Nana.</i>

11
00:01:13,640 --> 00:01:17,200
<i>I'd rather be an idiot than
have to live off a woman.</i>

12
00:01:17,200 --> 00:01:18,800
<i>It's our pink slip.</i>

13
00:01:18,800 --> 00:01:21,320
<i>Mom, don't tell them I got laid off.</i>

14
00:01:21,320 --> 00:01:22,520
<i>Let go.</i>

15
00:01:22,520 --> 00:01:23,880
<i>Where is she?</i>

16
00:01:23,880 --> 00:01:25,400
<i>Take me to her, please.</i>

17
00:01:26,640 --> 00:01:27,783
[2026]

18
00:01:27,783 --> 00:01:28,760
Go to school.

19
00:01:28,760 --> 00:01:29,800
[2013]
Go to school.

20
00:01:29,800 --> 00:01:31,760
Jump, hop!

21
00:01:32,984 --> 00:01:34,920
There, there...

22
00:01:34,920 --> 00:01:36,480
- Mom, Dad.
- Wow, good job...

23
00:01:36,480 --> 00:01:37,920
Danai and I are leaving now.

24
00:01:37,920 --> 00:01:38,800
Yes.

25
00:01:38,800 --> 00:01:40,170
- Go.
- Go.

26
00:01:40,170 --> 00:01:41,480
You're in Grade 12 now.

27
00:01:41,480 --> 00:01:42,880
Study hard,

28
00:01:42,880 --> 00:01:43,960
so you can go far.

29
00:01:43,960 --> 00:01:47,640
Yes, Dad. I'll get a doctoral degree.

30
00:01:47,640 --> 00:01:48,800
That's my girl.

31
00:01:48,800 --> 00:01:50,400
Now, now, it's time to go to school.

32
00:01:50,400 --> 00:01:51,560
Go, before you're late.

33
00:01:51,560 --> 00:01:52,840
Let's go, Danai.

34
00:01:52,840 --> 00:01:54,542
Take care of him.

35
00:01:54,542 --> 00:01:56,480
Go. Bye-bye.

36
00:01:56,480 --> 00:01:57,960
- Say bye-bye.
- Bye-bye.

37
00:01:57,960 --> 00:01:59,080
- Say bye-bye.
- Did you say goodbye?

38
00:01:59,080 --> 00:02:00,800
- Goodbye.
- Goodbye, go, go.

39
00:02:00,800 --> 00:02:03,480
- Let's go. I'll see you at the gym, Dad.
- Okay.

40
00:02:03,480 --> 00:02:04,560
Let's go.

41
00:02:09,360 --> 00:02:10,920
Dad...

42
00:02:10,920 --> 00:02:13,120
Ran knows that you want her
to get a good education.

43
00:02:13,120 --> 00:02:15,040
She won't forget it.

44
00:02:16,560 --> 00:02:19,520
Well, I can't help it.

45
00:02:19,520 --> 00:02:21,165
I just want them to have a good future.

46
00:02:21,165 --> 00:02:22,440
You're like this all the time.

47
00:02:22,440 --> 00:02:23,720
Come on, let's go eat.

48
00:02:23,720 --> 00:02:26,440
Okay? You'll be late.

49
00:02:26,440 --> 00:02:29,360
Come on, let's go.

50
00:02:29,360 --> 00:02:33,800
<i>♪ They will sacrifice every drop of
their blood to contribute to the nation ♪</i>

51
00:02:33,800 --> 00:02:39,120
<i>♪ Hail the nation of Thailand,
long last the victory, hurrah ♪</i>

52
00:02:42,640 --> 00:02:45,328
She's pretty, smart,

53
00:02:45,328 --> 00:02:47,440
and can do taekwondo, too.

54
00:02:47,440 --> 00:02:50,120
She's definitely a future
Thailand national youth team player.

55
00:02:50,120 --> 00:02:53,840
Oh, no wonder she was
the sports day president two years in a row.

56
00:02:53,840 --> 00:02:56,040
She's like an angel.

57
00:02:57,520 --> 00:03:00,440
Whoever gets to date her is so lucky.

58
00:03:00,440 --> 00:03:02,265
Do you think...

59
00:03:02,265 --> 00:03:04,148
I stand a chance?

60
00:03:04,148 --> 00:03:05,693
Can you shut up?

61
00:03:05,693 --> 00:03:07,453
Shit, Nilapia is here.

62
00:03:11,195 --> 00:03:12,660
My name is Saengnil.

63
00:03:12,660 --> 00:03:14,300
Not Nilapia.

64
00:03:15,600 --> 00:03:17,080
I'm sorry.

65
00:03:18,640 --> 00:03:20,440
Fuck, how did she hear me?

66
00:03:25,840 --> 00:03:27,400
Yai.

67
00:03:32,227 --> 00:03:35,132
Next, we will award scholarships to

68
00:03:35,132 --> 00:03:37,877
students who have achieved
academic excellence.

69
00:03:37,877 --> 00:03:41,822
I will start with students in Grade 10

70
00:03:41,822 --> 00:03:45,760
and continue through Grade 12.

71
00:03:45,760 --> 00:03:48,345
Grade 10,

72
00:03:48,345 --> 00:03:50,850
the Academic Excellence Scholarship

73
00:03:50,850 --> 00:03:54,840
goes to... Miss Palada Ploikrathok.

74
00:03:54,840 --> 00:03:56,400
[Scholarship Award Ceremony
Honoring Academic Excellence]

75
00:03:56,400 --> 00:03:59,216
[Academic Year 2013]

76
00:03:59,216 --> 00:04:02,121
Grade 12,

77
00:04:02,121 --> 00:04:05,520
the first-place Academic Excellence Scholarship

78
00:04:05,520 --> 00:04:07,361
goes to...

79
00:04:07,361 --> 00:04:09,920
"Miss Daran Kaewkaruna."

80
00:04:09,920 --> 00:04:13,200
Miss Daran Kaewkaruna.

81
00:04:19,560 --> 00:04:24,000
[Congratulations to Miss Daran Kaewkaruna]

82
00:04:24,000 --> 00:04:26,440
Second place goes to...

83
00:04:26,440 --> 00:04:28,160
"Miss Natasha Sahaphet."

84
00:04:28,160 --> 00:04:31,000
Miss Natasha Sahaphet.

85
00:04:32,120 --> 00:04:33,200
How did you know?

86
00:04:33,200 --> 00:04:35,105
Do you have a third eye?

87
00:04:35,105 --> 00:04:38,570
It's like this every year.
Why would this year be any different?

88
00:04:38,570 --> 00:04:40,290
Well, you're right.

89
00:04:45,880 --> 00:04:47,665
Why did your girl do that?

90
00:04:47,665 --> 00:04:49,265
Take care of her for me.

91
00:04:50,760 --> 00:04:53,000
Stop it, she isn't "my girl."

92
00:04:54,600 --> 00:04:59,120
[Congratulations to Miss Natasha Sahaphet]

93
00:05:12,640 --> 00:05:13,800
You should've just...

94
00:05:13,800 --> 00:05:16,320
kicked her in the neck and knocked her out.

95
00:05:16,320 --> 00:05:19,040
And when she wakes up,
she'll be a new person.

96
00:05:19,040 --> 00:05:21,000
I'll get expelled from school if I do that.

97
00:05:21,000 --> 00:05:23,640
That'd ruin my life as an honors student.

98
00:05:23,640 --> 00:05:25,280
Just let it go.

99
00:05:25,280 --> 00:05:28,320
If I keep it cool,
she'll get bored and stop provoking me soon.

100
00:05:28,320 --> 00:05:30,120
Just one more year.

101
00:05:30,120 --> 00:05:33,268
Fine, Miss Goody Two-Shoes.

102
00:05:33,268 --> 00:05:34,960
- Oh, did you know?
- Hm?

103
00:05:34,960 --> 00:05:37,600
Gramps is actually in our class.

104
00:05:37,600 --> 00:05:38,960
"Gramps"?

105
00:05:39,760 --> 00:05:44,600
Do you ever know anything
besides textbooks and taekwondo?

106
00:05:45,840 --> 00:05:47,960
It's Yai!

107
00:05:47,960 --> 00:05:50,527
Why didn't you just say his name?

108
00:05:50,527 --> 00:05:53,240
Wasn't he an exchange student
in the U.S. last year?

109
00:05:53,240 --> 00:05:53,960
Yep.

110
00:05:53,960 --> 00:05:56,440
He's pretty popular. Why call him Gramps?

111
00:05:56,440 --> 00:05:58,640
He's only a year older than us, isn't he?

112
00:05:58,640 --> 00:06:01,440
No, no, no. Not just one year.

113
00:06:01,440 --> 00:06:03,800
He repeated a year back in primary school.

114
00:06:03,800 --> 00:06:05,920
Then he spent another year
on an exchange program.

115
00:06:05,920 --> 00:06:08,807
That means he's two years older than me.

116
00:06:08,807 --> 00:06:10,480
You started school early, yeah?

117
00:06:10,480 --> 00:06:13,280
You're 17, and he's 20.

118
00:06:13,280 --> 00:06:16,200
That means he's three years older than you.

119
00:06:16,200 --> 00:06:17,259
So?

120
00:06:17,259 --> 00:06:18,160
What?

121
00:06:18,160 --> 00:06:21,840
He's in our class now, you know?

122
00:06:29,880 --> 00:06:32,105
You didn't hear us, right?

123
00:06:32,105 --> 00:06:34,545
I'm old but not deaf.

124
00:06:37,040 --> 00:06:39,120
- You goose!
- You!

125
00:06:39,120 --> 00:06:41,640
Yai! Yai! Ow.

126
00:06:41,640 --> 00:06:43,080
- Yai! Yai...
- Nooch.

127
00:06:43,080 --> 00:06:45,400
Stop, the teacher might see us.

128
00:06:54,280 --> 00:06:56,280
This isn't over.

129
00:06:59,320 --> 00:07:00,640
Hey, that's fine with me.

130
00:07:00,640 --> 00:07:03,000
- Let's go.
- I haven't eaten there for a while now.

131
00:07:06,600 --> 00:07:09,000
Nooch?

132
00:07:09,000 --> 00:07:10,880
Weren't our bags here?

133
00:07:16,267 --> 00:07:18,387
Aren't we sitting too close to the front?

134
00:07:19,941 --> 00:07:22,040
Actually, we weren't supposed to sit here,

135
00:07:22,040 --> 00:07:25,505
but someone likes putting
other people's bags up front.

136
00:07:25,505 --> 00:07:27,080
Nasty.

137
00:07:27,080 --> 00:07:28,960
Who are you calling nasty?

138
00:07:28,960 --> 00:07:31,000
If it doesn't apply to you, why get offended?

139
00:07:38,400 --> 00:07:40,960
What are you looking at, Miss No. 1 Student?

140
00:07:40,960 --> 00:07:42,745
Are you mad?

141
00:07:42,745 --> 00:07:46,680
Hey, wait... what did you just say?

142
00:07:47,480 --> 00:07:49,480
Are you... jealous of my friend?

143
00:07:49,480 --> 00:07:50,600
Why?

144
00:07:50,600 --> 00:07:52,840
Does being in second place
hurt your ego that much?

145
00:07:52,840 --> 00:07:53,560
Hey!

146
00:07:53,560 --> 00:07:54,680
Nooch.

147
00:07:54,680 --> 00:07:56,000
Enough, don't fight.

148
00:07:56,000 --> 00:07:57,440
We can sit here.

149
00:07:57,440 --> 00:07:58,540
Oh?

150
00:07:58,540 --> 00:08:00,680
How nice of you.

151
00:08:00,680 --> 00:08:02,440
I'm not trying to be nice.

152
00:08:02,440 --> 00:08:05,360
I just don't like starting a fight.

153
00:08:11,541 --> 00:08:13,760
Is the teacher here? Hello.

154
00:08:13,760 --> 00:08:15,640
Alright!

155
00:08:15,640 --> 00:08:18,200
What are you all laughing at? Go to your seats.

156
00:08:18,200 --> 00:08:20,880
What was the commotion?
I heard people laughing just now.

157
00:08:20,880 --> 00:08:21,880
Mr. Saharat?

158
00:08:21,880 --> 00:08:23,400
It's not me.

159
00:09:13,240 --> 00:09:15,225
Have you arrived?

160
00:09:15,225 --> 00:09:16,745
I'll be there right away.

161
00:09:17,875 --> 00:09:19,555
Yai.

162
00:09:21,348 --> 00:09:23,653
Can you drop me off at home?

163
00:09:23,653 --> 00:09:27,398
My family's chauffeur is sick,
so I have to go home by myself.

164
00:09:27,398 --> 00:09:29,423
But I don't want to take a taxi.

165
00:09:29,423 --> 00:09:30,968
I'm scared.

166
00:09:30,968 --> 00:09:32,582
Yai.

167
00:09:32,582 --> 00:09:34,280
Can you drop me off?

168
00:09:34,280 --> 00:09:36,160
Please?

169
00:09:39,200 --> 00:09:40,960
Thank you.

170
00:09:42,588 --> 00:09:45,754
- Please take Nana home.
- Yes, Mr. Yai.

171
00:09:45,754 --> 00:09:47,000
Yai!

172
00:09:47,000 --> 00:09:48,957
Yai, where are you going?

173
00:09:48,957 --> 00:09:50,142
Yai!

174
00:09:50,142 --> 00:09:52,007
Yai!

175
00:09:52,007 --> 00:09:53,487
Yai!

176
00:10:13,320 --> 00:10:15,425
Oh, Ran.

177
00:10:15,425 --> 00:10:18,200
You have to control your heart
and use your brain, alright?

178
00:10:18,200 --> 00:10:20,320
Use your head like when you're studying.

179
00:10:20,320 --> 00:10:23,882
And keep your heart in a drawer at home.

180
00:10:23,882 --> 00:10:25,280
Why are you lecturing me?

181
00:10:25,280 --> 00:10:26,880
I'm not going to have a boyfriend yet.

182
00:10:26,880 --> 00:10:28,480
I want to wait until after graduation.

183
00:10:28,480 --> 00:10:31,200
And it's not like I have anyone
flirting with me.

184
00:10:31,200 --> 00:10:33,280
Who said you don't?

185
00:10:33,280 --> 00:10:34,280
You do.

186
00:10:34,280 --> 00:10:37,640
But I scared the pants off them all.

187
00:10:38,720 --> 00:10:39,960
Why?

188
00:10:39,960 --> 00:10:42,025
Well, my friend is this pretty.

189
00:10:42,025 --> 00:10:44,320
Why would I let some simpletons
flirt with you?

190
00:10:44,320 --> 00:10:48,970
I'll be your scanner
who screens the men for you.

191
00:10:48,970 --> 00:10:50,570
Thanks.

192
00:10:54,120 --> 00:10:55,400
Hey, Nooch.

193
00:10:57,640 --> 00:10:58,800
Nooch.

194
00:10:58,800 --> 00:11:00,718
I forgot to bring my taekwondo bag.

195
00:11:00,718 --> 00:11:02,543
I have the uniform in there.

196
00:11:02,543 --> 00:11:03,648
Oh...

197
00:11:03,648 --> 00:11:06,400
You carry too many bags around, you know?

198
00:11:06,400 --> 00:11:09,145
I have to take all the books
I brought to school back home.

199
00:11:09,145 --> 00:11:09,960
Yeah, yeah.

200
00:11:09,960 --> 00:11:12,440
Go get it yourself then.
I don't want to walk up the stairs.

201
00:11:12,440 --> 00:11:13,840
I'll leave these with you for a bit.

202
00:11:13,840 --> 00:11:15,111
Be right back.

203
00:11:17,400 --> 00:11:19,040
Okay?

204
00:11:21,280 --> 00:11:23,320
Why do you have to bring so many things?

205
00:11:42,760 --> 00:11:44,800
Ran!

206
00:11:44,800 --> 00:11:45,800
Ran!

207
00:11:45,800 --> 00:11:46,720
- Ran!
- Ran!

208
00:11:46,720 --> 00:11:47,880
Ran, wait!

209
00:11:47,880 --> 00:11:48,800
Ran!

210
00:11:48,800 --> 00:11:49,640
Wait!

211
00:11:49,640 --> 00:11:51,720
- Ran, come back!
- Hey!

212
00:11:51,720 --> 00:11:54,200
- Please calm down!
- Ran!

213
00:11:56,960 --> 00:11:58,320
Ran, wait!

214
00:11:58,320 --> 00:11:59,920
Wait for me, Ran!

215
00:12:00,963 --> 00:12:02,996
Please don't tell our teacher about this.

216
00:12:02,996 --> 00:12:04,745
I'm begging you. Please.

217
00:12:05,560 --> 00:12:07,545
Please, Ran.

218
00:12:07,545 --> 00:12:10,370
If you tell them, we'll both get expelled.

219
00:12:10,370 --> 00:12:12,480
Then why didn't you think
of the consequences?

220
00:12:12,480 --> 00:12:14,640
And most importantly, that's my desk.

221
00:12:14,640 --> 00:12:17,680
Please, Ran.
Don't tell our teacher about this.

222
00:12:19,400 --> 00:12:21,705
Daran will not tell anyone about this.

223
00:12:21,705 --> 00:12:23,225
- Yai!
- Yai!

224
00:12:24,594 --> 00:12:26,099
Dress properly.

225
00:12:26,099 --> 00:12:28,964
And pick a different place next time.

226
00:12:28,964 --> 00:12:31,924
Or this poor honors student's heart
might not be able to take it.

227
00:12:33,720 --> 00:12:35,600
They are young and full of hormones,

228
00:12:35,600 --> 00:12:37,705
so they are a bit reckless.

229
00:12:37,705 --> 00:12:39,385
Give them a chance.

230
00:12:44,866 --> 00:12:49,836
Promise me you won't do this at school again.

231
00:12:49,836 --> 00:12:51,760
- We promise.
- We promise.

232
00:12:51,760 --> 00:12:53,200
Now go.

233
00:12:53,200 --> 00:12:55,920
- Thank you, Yai.
- Thank you, Yai.

234
00:13:34,480 --> 00:13:37,120
So... How was the live show?

235
00:13:37,120 --> 00:13:38,560
Was it fun?

236
00:13:38,560 --> 00:13:39,800
Wait.

237
00:13:42,240 --> 00:13:44,625
You still look pale.

238
00:13:44,625 --> 00:13:46,690
Can you walk?

239
00:13:46,690 --> 00:13:49,155
Or do you need me to carry you downstairs?

240
00:13:49,155 --> 00:13:51,440
Can you stop being annoying?

241
00:13:51,440 --> 00:13:53,720
Wow, you can be quite fierce, huh?

242
00:13:53,720 --> 00:13:56,960
But you looked very pale just now.

243
00:13:56,960 --> 00:13:59,680
Seriously, do you hate me or something?

244
00:13:59,680 --> 00:14:02,040
Why do you have to be so sarcastic?

245
00:14:05,120 --> 00:14:06,480
I don't hate you.

246
00:14:09,107 --> 00:14:10,387
I like you.

247
00:14:23,670 --> 00:14:24,800
I'll flirt with you.

248
00:14:24,800 --> 00:14:26,160
No.

249
00:14:26,160 --> 00:14:27,200
I will.

250
00:14:27,200 --> 00:14:29,080
You won't win.

251
00:14:30,011 --> 00:14:31,531
Want me to try?

252
00:14:38,400 --> 00:14:42,400
[2013]

253
00:14:42,400 --> 00:14:43,480
[2026]

254
00:15:01,586 --> 00:15:03,066
This way, please.

255
00:16:37,095 --> 00:16:40,720
Sam can only pair with Luknut!

256
00:16:40,720 --> 00:16:42,920
Did you see a woman in jeans and a blue shirt,

257
00:16:42,920 --> 00:16:46,840
with mid-back-length hair,
and carrying a cream-colored bag?

258
00:16:46,840 --> 00:16:48,920
[Cutie Sam, Sweety Nut]
No, sir.

259
00:16:48,920 --> 00:16:52,960
Sam can only pair with Luknut!

260
00:16:52,960 --> 00:16:56,640
Sam can only pair with Luknut!

261
00:16:56,640 --> 00:16:58,520
Sam can only pair with Luknut!

262
00:16:58,520 --> 00:17:00,600
It's time, sir.

263
00:17:00,600 --> 00:17:04,400
Sam can only pair with Luknut!

264
00:17:04,400 --> 00:17:08,560
Sam can only pair with Luknut!

265
00:17:08,560 --> 00:17:12,280
Sam can only pair with Luknut!

266
00:17:12,280 --> 00:17:14,560
Fire this security team.

267
00:17:19,000 --> 00:17:23,360
Sam can only pair with Luknut!

268
00:17:25,320 --> 00:17:26,856
Right this way.

269
00:17:26,856 --> 00:17:28,601
Why are you detaining me?

270
00:17:28,601 --> 00:17:31,184
You made it seem like I'm a criminal!

271
00:17:31,184 --> 00:17:32,464
Dao!

272
00:17:34,402 --> 00:17:35,787
Hello.

273
00:17:35,787 --> 00:17:39,052
Well, this security guard told me

274
00:17:39,052 --> 00:17:41,877
to come pick up my sister,
but he didn't tell me what she did.

275
00:17:41,877 --> 00:17:44,342
I was just fulfilling my duty as a fan.

276
00:17:44,342 --> 00:17:45,635
Dao!

277
00:17:47,400 --> 00:17:49,120
<i>Sam can only pair with Luknut!</i>

278
00:17:49,120 --> 00:17:52,320
[Cutie Sam, Sweety Nut]
<i>Sam can only pair with Luknut!</i>

279
00:17:52,320 --> 00:17:55,120
<i>Sam can only pair with Luknut!</i>

280
00:17:55,120 --> 00:17:57,160
<i>- Dao!
- What?</i>

281
00:17:57,160 --> 00:18:00,617
<i>Pangya's fan account
posted a fitting photo with Sam.</i>

282
00:18:00,617 --> 00:18:01,680
<i>Where?</i>

283
00:18:01,680 --> 00:18:02,760
[New Next Empire]

284
00:18:03,623 --> 00:18:06,440
<i>We've been shouting ourselves hoarse,
and they're still not listening!</i>

285
00:18:06,440 --> 00:18:08,040
<i>What should we do, Dao?</i>

286
00:18:08,040 --> 00:18:11,120
<i>Sam can only pair with Luknut!</i>

287
00:18:11,120 --> 00:18:14,160
<i>Sam can only pair with Luknut!</i>

288
00:18:14,160 --> 00:18:20,120
<i>Sam can only pair with Luknut!</i>

289
00:18:20,120 --> 00:18:24,968
<i>Sam can only pair with Luknut!</i>

290
00:19:11,800 --> 00:19:13,880
[Executive Chairman]

291
00:19:25,880 --> 00:19:28,400
[Executive Chairman]

292
00:19:35,240 --> 00:19:38,265
<i>Sam's fan club is currently protesting.</i>

293
00:19:38,265 --> 00:19:39,760
<i>How did you get in here?</i>

294
00:19:39,760 --> 00:19:41,280
<i>I just walked in.</i>

295
00:19:41,280 --> 00:19:42,785
<i>Aren't there any security guards?</i>

296
00:19:42,785 --> 00:19:44,570
<i>They all went downstairs.</i>

297
00:19:44,570 --> 00:19:46,438
<i>Little miss, please leave.</i>

298
00:19:46,438 --> 00:19:47,360
<i>No!</i>

299
00:19:47,360 --> 00:19:49,400
<i>I have an important matter
to discuss with the chairman.</i>

300
00:19:49,400 --> 00:19:52,321
<i>You can't. Let's go.</i>

301
00:19:52,321 --> 00:19:53,960
<i>If I don't get to speak with him,</i>

302
00:19:53,960 --> 00:19:55,465
<i>I won't be going anywhere.</i>

303
00:19:55,465 --> 00:19:58,210
<i>This old man needs to listen
to the voices of Sam's fans,</i>

304
00:19:58,210 --> 00:20:02,220
<i>instead of sitting in his ivory tower
and ignoring all our feedback.</i>

305
00:20:02,220 --> 00:20:03,280
<i>Little miss...</i>

306
00:20:03,280 --> 00:20:04,600
<i>That's enough.</i>

307
00:20:04,600 --> 00:20:06,625
<i>Tell security to escort her out.</i>

308
00:20:06,625 --> 00:20:07,680
<i>Yes, sir.</i>

309
00:20:07,680 --> 00:20:10,640
<i>But will you be alright
if I leave you here with her?</i>

310
00:20:15,778 --> 00:20:17,483
<i>She's that tiny.</i>

311
00:20:17,483 --> 00:20:19,243
<i>What can she do?</i>

312
00:20:26,337 --> 00:20:28,000
<i>So, tell me...</i>

313
00:20:28,000 --> 00:20:30,354
<i>What is it that I need to hear?</i>

314
00:20:30,354 --> 00:20:34,360
<i>Not just hear, but you have
to listen and take it to heart.</i>

315
00:20:34,360 --> 00:20:36,600
<i>If you still have one, that is.</i>

316
00:20:38,400 --> 00:20:40,825
<i>Do you think I'm heartless?</i>

317
00:20:40,825 --> 00:20:43,985
<i>If you had one, today's fitting
wouldn't have happened.</i>

318
00:20:44,983 --> 00:20:46,800
<i>Just get to the point</i>

319
00:20:46,800 --> 00:20:51,185
<i>before security takes you away
and you lose your chance forever.</i>

320
00:20:51,185 --> 00:20:52,720
<i>The right chemistry between two people</i>

321
00:20:52,720 --> 00:20:54,800
<i>is hard to come by.</i>

322
00:20:54,800 --> 00:20:55,960
<i>Just like Sam and Luknut,</i>

323
00:20:55,960 --> 00:20:57,837
<i>who should be kept together.</i>

324
00:20:57,837 --> 00:21:00,080
<i>He's not your lab rat
to pair with just anyone</i>

325
00:21:00,080 --> 00:21:01,865
<i>who isn't born for him.</i>

326
00:21:01,865 --> 00:21:04,120
<i>We aren't some generic, senseless fans.</i>

327
00:21:04,120 --> 00:21:06,920
<i>We've already seen
Sam at an event with Pangya,</i>

328
00:21:06,920 --> 00:21:08,792
<i>and we found that</i>

329
00:21:08,792 --> 00:21:12,480
<i>it won't work!</i>

330
00:21:12,480 --> 00:21:16,000
<i>But you guys are too stubborn because
you want to push your own actors.</i>

331
00:21:16,000 --> 00:21:18,480
<i>If the project flops with only
your own actors in it, that's fine.</i>

332
00:21:18,480 --> 00:21:21,160
<i>But if you drag Sam down with them...</i>

333
00:21:24,320 --> 00:21:25,560
[Executive Chairman]

334
00:21:25,560 --> 00:21:28,720
<i>I won't allow it!</i>

335
00:21:28,720 --> 00:21:31,720
<i>I won't allow it!</i>

336
00:21:31,720 --> 00:21:33,320
<i>I won't allow it!</i>

337
00:21:33,320 --> 00:21:36,680
<i>Old man, you're a chump! You! Are! Out!</i>

338
00:21:41,200 --> 00:21:44,825
<i>I won't allow it!</i>

339
00:21:44,825 --> 00:21:47,345
<i>I won't allow it!</i>

340
00:21:50,880 --> 00:21:53,105
That's what...

341
00:21:53,105 --> 00:21:55,810
It's just like she said.

342
00:21:55,810 --> 00:21:56,646
So...

343
00:21:56,646 --> 00:21:59,791
Dao got to meet the chairman?

344
00:21:59,791 --> 00:22:00,856
Yes.

345
00:22:00,856 --> 00:22:04,240
If... my subordinates hadn't
gotten there in time,

346
00:22:04,240 --> 00:22:06,280
she might not have just complained.

347
00:22:06,280 --> 00:22:08,105
I'm afraid

348
00:22:08,105 --> 00:22:09,840
she might have done something out of line.

349
00:22:09,840 --> 00:22:12,920
I'm not going to bite his ear off.

350
00:22:12,920 --> 00:22:14,190
Dao!

351
00:22:15,080 --> 00:22:18,290
But if your chump manager
still doesn't listen to me,

352
00:22:18,290 --> 00:22:19,730
then maybe I will.

353
00:22:21,072 --> 00:22:24,560
Can you stop saying whatever comes to mind?

354
00:22:24,560 --> 00:22:26,276
Fine!

355
00:22:28,400 --> 00:22:31,080
My employer won't press charges this time.

356
00:22:31,080 --> 00:22:33,865
But if it happens again,

357
00:22:33,865 --> 00:22:35,865
prepare to get sued.

358
00:22:37,612 --> 00:22:39,597
I'm truly sorry.

359
00:22:39,597 --> 00:22:41,960
This won't happen again.

360
00:22:41,960 --> 00:22:44,786
And thank you again.

361
00:22:44,786 --> 00:22:46,120
Then...

362
00:22:46,120 --> 00:22:48,225
I'll be taking her with me.

363
00:22:48,225 --> 00:22:49,585
Wait.

364
00:22:50,657 --> 00:22:52,977
Please sign this form.

365
00:22:54,720 --> 00:22:56,080
Go on.

366
00:23:05,680 --> 00:23:07,600
I'll lead the way.

367
00:23:16,558 --> 00:23:19,720
Why are kids these days like this?
They talk nonstop.

368
00:23:19,720 --> 00:23:22,920
Oh gosh, I'm going to faint.

369
00:23:22,920 --> 00:23:24,760
Do you want me to call the ambulance, sir?

370
00:23:24,760 --> 00:23:26,800
Ambulance, my ass. I'm not dying!

371
00:23:30,280 --> 00:23:33,480
Do you have feelings for my sister?
You keep staring at her.

372
00:23:33,480 --> 00:23:35,252
Dao, when will you stop?

373
00:23:35,252 --> 00:23:36,560
Stop what?

374
00:23:36,560 --> 00:23:39,200
Stop talking without thinking.

375
00:23:41,440 --> 00:23:43,305
You got it wrong.

376
00:23:43,305 --> 00:23:45,705
Your sister just looks familiar to me.

377
00:23:48,160 --> 00:23:50,985
You really don't remember?

378
00:23:50,985 --> 00:23:53,610
We didn't just meet here.

379
00:23:53,610 --> 00:23:56,635
But we'd met... long before this.

380
00:23:59,080 --> 00:24:01,040
I'm sorry, but...

381
00:24:01,040 --> 00:24:04,423
I meet a lot of people,
so I might not remember everyone.

382
00:24:04,423 --> 00:24:06,440
We might have met at a cafe.

383
00:24:06,440 --> 00:24:08,640
I work there from morning to afternoon.

384
00:24:08,640 --> 00:24:10,400
Or maybe you saw me at the minimart.

385
00:24:10,400 --> 00:24:13,120
I work there from afternoon to midnight.

386
00:24:13,120 --> 00:24:16,953
Or... you might have bought soy milk
at my house early in the morning.

387
00:24:16,953 --> 00:24:20,453
Maybe you had my mom iron your clothes,
and Ran was there to help.

388
00:24:20,453 --> 00:24:21,920
And when do you sleep?

389
00:24:21,920 --> 00:24:24,475
Well, I sleep when I can.

390
00:24:26,000 --> 00:24:28,120
Why do you have to work so many jobs?

391
00:24:29,473 --> 00:24:31,738
Ran provides for our whole family.

392
00:24:31,738 --> 00:24:34,560
Well... is there a job here...

393
00:24:34,560 --> 00:24:36,790
that isn't too demanding
and pays around 25,000 baht?

394
00:24:36,790 --> 00:24:38,200
So Ran can apply for that job.

395
00:24:38,200 --> 00:24:41,640
And I'll visit often,
so maybe I'll get to meet Sam.

396
00:24:41,640 --> 00:24:42,800
- Dao.
- Dao!

397
00:24:42,800 --> 00:24:46,200
Okay, I'll stop. End of conversation.

398
00:24:47,520 --> 00:24:49,160
You can send us off here.

399
00:24:49,160 --> 00:24:51,120
Is the exit that way?

400
00:24:51,120 --> 00:24:52,345
Yes.

401
00:24:52,345 --> 00:24:53,880
Thank you.

402
00:24:53,880 --> 00:24:55,360
Let's go.

403
00:25:04,600 --> 00:25:06,320
Yes, Ms. Wan.

404
00:25:06,320 --> 00:25:07,320
Thank you.

405
00:25:07,320 --> 00:25:08,720
Goodbye.

406
00:25:11,000 --> 00:25:13,145
How did it go, Mr. Alex?
Is everything in order?

407
00:25:13,145 --> 00:25:14,240
Yes.

408
00:25:14,240 --> 00:25:15,760
Is there a problem?

409
00:25:15,760 --> 00:25:17,440
She told me...

410
00:25:17,440 --> 00:25:21,545
this entire security team has been fired.

411
00:25:23,840 --> 00:25:25,320
We need a new team.

412
00:25:25,320 --> 00:25:26,750
Why?

413
00:25:26,750 --> 00:25:28,040
She didn't tell me.

414
00:25:28,040 --> 00:25:29,360
But I think it's...

415
00:25:29,360 --> 00:25:30,800
F.U.C.K.

416
00:25:30,800 --> 00:25:33,265
Hey, that's too harsh.

417
00:25:33,265 --> 00:25:36,920
Focus. Understand. Control. Knowledge.

418
00:25:36,920 --> 00:25:38,200
Oh.

419
00:25:38,200 --> 00:25:40,480
Well, I think this is about

420
00:25:40,480 --> 00:25:43,960
how we couldn't control the crowd,

421
00:25:43,960 --> 00:25:47,280
letting that girl break into
the chairman's office.

422
00:25:51,600 --> 00:25:52,880
Are you stressed?

423
00:25:54,169 --> 00:25:55,280
Not at all.

424
00:25:55,280 --> 00:25:56,480
Really?

425
00:25:56,480 --> 00:25:58,320
Well, I'm really stressed.

426
00:25:58,320 --> 00:25:59,600
Very stressed.

427
00:26:17,120 --> 00:26:18,200
Good.

428
00:26:18,200 --> 00:26:21,090
We'll do a close-up next.

429
00:26:21,090 --> 00:26:22,400
This pair...

430
00:26:22,400 --> 00:26:24,720
has great chemistry, don't you think?

431
00:26:24,720 --> 00:26:27,840
They do. I'll give them a try.

432
00:26:27,840 --> 00:26:29,080
This is great.

433
00:26:29,080 --> 00:26:30,880
I think this will be a hit.

434
00:26:30,880 --> 00:26:33,346
Yes, certainly.

435
00:26:35,940 --> 00:26:38,445
Can I go to the restroom for a bit?

436
00:26:38,445 --> 00:26:40,590
Of course, Mr. Sam.

437
00:26:40,590 --> 00:26:41,855
Everyone,

438
00:26:42,615 --> 00:26:44,960
let's take a ten-minute break.

439
00:26:44,960 --> 00:26:47,800
Let's go check the set. Please excuse me.

440
00:26:55,089 --> 00:26:56,409
Nana.

441
00:27:01,443 --> 00:27:03,123
Ms. Natasha.

442
00:27:05,491 --> 00:27:06,636
Yes?

443
00:27:06,636 --> 00:27:09,181
Have they all left?

444
00:27:09,181 --> 00:27:10,486
They all left

445
00:27:10,486 --> 00:27:13,471
because they were told
they'd be charged with trespassing.

446
00:27:13,471 --> 00:27:15,320
Those narrow-minded people.

447
00:27:15,320 --> 00:27:18,425
Just wait until
Sam and Pangya's TV series airs.

448
00:27:18,425 --> 00:27:20,640
They'll thank me later.

449
00:27:20,640 --> 00:27:23,680
Your vision is always splendid.

450
00:27:26,298 --> 00:27:28,043
I'll leave the rest to you.

451
00:27:28,043 --> 00:27:29,800
Handle the issues.

452
00:27:29,800 --> 00:27:32,440
If it's not a big deal, don't call me.

453
00:27:32,440 --> 00:27:33,720
Yes.

454
00:27:37,433 --> 00:27:38,526
Kaew,

455
00:27:39,280 --> 00:27:42,200
where is Ms. Natasha
getting the confidence from

456
00:27:42,200 --> 00:27:44,080
that this pair will work out?

457
00:27:44,080 --> 00:27:47,040
Their chemistry is completely off.
Isn't that right?

458
00:27:47,040 --> 00:27:49,600
- Yeah.
- Right?

459
00:27:49,600 --> 00:27:51,600
From birth.

460
00:27:51,600 --> 00:27:53,640
She's always been like this.

461
00:27:54,771 --> 00:27:56,636
You always nag like an old woman, Ran.

462
00:27:56,636 --> 00:27:58,501
I got it already.

463
00:27:58,501 --> 00:28:00,526
How could I not nag?

464
00:28:00,526 --> 00:28:02,431
You made me worried.

465
00:28:02,431 --> 00:28:03,951
Ran...

466
00:28:11,475 --> 00:28:13,880
<i>Does being in second place
hurt your ego that much?</i>

467
00:28:13,880 --> 00:28:14,640
<i>Hey!</i>

468
00:28:14,640 --> 00:28:15,840
<i>Nooch.</i>

469
00:28:15,840 --> 00:28:17,120
<i>Enough, don't fight.</i>

470
00:28:17,120 --> 00:28:18,720
<i>We can sit here.</i>

471
00:28:18,720 --> 00:28:19,800
<i>Oh?</i>

472
00:28:19,800 --> 00:28:21,880
<i>How nice of you.</i>

473
00:28:21,880 --> 00:28:23,720
<i>I'm not trying to be nice.</i>

474
00:28:23,720 --> 00:28:26,357
<i>I just don't like starting a fight.</i>

475
00:28:33,240 --> 00:28:35,640
The taxi is here. Come on, let's go.

476
00:28:51,560 --> 00:28:54,025
Oops. Sorry, Ran.

477
00:28:54,025 --> 00:28:55,705
Why are you here?

478
00:28:57,148 --> 00:28:58,533
Are you together?

479
00:28:58,533 --> 00:29:00,000
- No!
- Yes!

480
00:29:00,000 --> 00:29:01,080
Just go, please.

481
00:29:01,080 --> 00:29:03,825
I'll pay you double.

482
00:29:03,825 --> 00:29:05,730
Roger that, sir!

483
00:29:05,730 --> 00:29:07,080
Stop here. We're getting out.

484
00:29:07,080 --> 00:29:09,000
Yes, yes, yes.

485
00:29:15,199 --> 00:29:18,040
Don't shout. Sam might get startled.

486
00:29:18,040 --> 00:29:19,240
Keep going, Uncle.

487
00:29:19,240 --> 00:29:20,520
Sam?

488
00:29:28,026 --> 00:29:29,746
Do you remember me?

489
00:29:31,482 --> 00:29:33,347
Why are you even here?

490
00:29:33,347 --> 00:29:35,707
Well...

491
00:29:37,106 --> 00:29:39,800
You're the girl who went...
into the chairman's office?

492
00:29:39,800 --> 00:29:41,240
That's me.

493
00:29:41,240 --> 00:29:43,800
Don't dig your nails into me!

494
00:29:43,800 --> 00:29:45,600
Okay.

495
00:29:46,691 --> 00:29:48,451
What are you doing here?

496
00:29:50,132 --> 00:29:55,222
I wanted to thank her
for liking and supporting me.

497
00:29:55,222 --> 00:29:57,207
Actually, I...

498
00:29:57,207 --> 00:29:59,912
felt the same way she and my fans did,

499
00:29:59,912 --> 00:30:03,000
but my voice wasn't loud enough.

500
00:30:03,000 --> 00:30:06,185
Did they pay you to keep quiet about it?

501
00:30:06,185 --> 00:30:07,770
Don't say that.

502
00:30:07,770 --> 00:30:10,770
You'll hurt his feelings.

503
00:30:12,120 --> 00:30:13,400
Are you done?

504
00:30:13,400 --> 00:30:15,000
Not yet.

505
00:30:15,000 --> 00:30:17,880
I was planning to take her all the way home.

506
00:30:19,836 --> 00:30:21,036
Sounds good?

507
00:30:43,960 --> 00:30:45,825
Meeting like this,

508
00:30:45,825 --> 00:30:48,185
if it isn't destiny, then what is?

509
00:30:57,388 --> 00:30:59,148
Hello?

510
00:31:01,160 --> 00:31:04,000
I had an upset stomach.
I'll go right back inside.

511
00:31:04,000 --> 00:31:05,240
Yes, yes.

512
00:31:09,467 --> 00:31:11,612
Where even am I?

513
00:31:11,612 --> 00:31:14,237
[Executive Chairman Advisor]

514
00:31:14,237 --> 00:31:16,077
I saw her come here.

515
00:31:17,360 --> 00:31:19,320
I never thought I'd see her again.

516
00:31:19,320 --> 00:31:21,560
What does she want, Auntie?

517
00:31:22,840 --> 00:31:24,240
How should I know?

518
00:31:24,240 --> 00:31:27,145
Auntie, didn't you say

519
00:31:27,145 --> 00:31:29,240
she wouldn't show her face around me anymore?

520
00:31:29,240 --> 00:31:30,880
But now she's right under my nose.

521
00:31:30,880 --> 00:31:33,604
Isn't this a little too much?

522
00:31:33,604 --> 00:31:35,829
Does Yai know about this?

523
00:31:35,829 --> 00:31:37,094
I don't know.

524
00:31:37,094 --> 00:31:38,934
I haven't talked to him.

525
00:32:34,240 --> 00:32:36,720
<i>It's all over your hand.</i>

526
00:32:36,720 --> 00:32:38,865
<i>Is it good?</i>

527
00:32:38,865 --> 00:32:40,990
<i>- Ran.
- Wipe it off.</i>

528
00:32:41,680 --> 00:32:43,160
<i>Hello, sir.</i>

529
00:32:44,962 --> 00:32:48,772
<i>Dad, this is Yai, the one I told you about.</i>

530
00:32:48,772 --> 00:32:50,880
<i>Why are you not in the house?</i>

531
00:32:50,880 --> 00:32:52,960
<i>Why give people something to gossip about?</i>

532
00:33:01,720 --> 00:33:04,640
<i>Hey, what's the rush?</i>

533
00:33:05,933 --> 00:33:07,638
<i>I'm cheering myself up.</i>

534
00:33:07,638 --> 00:33:10,543
<i>Your dad looked really mad at me.</i>

535
00:33:10,543 --> 00:33:12,368
<i>If you make me cry,</i>

536
00:33:12,368 --> 00:33:14,113
<i>he won't just be mad at you.</i>

537
00:33:14,113 --> 00:33:16,793
<i>He'll slam you to
the ground and break your back.</i>

538
00:33:18,379 --> 00:33:19,859
<i>Are you teasing me?</i>

539
00:33:21,490 --> 00:33:23,730
<i>Come on, let's get inside.</i>

540
00:34:07,920 --> 00:34:09,560
Hello.

541
00:34:09,560 --> 00:34:11,585
Who are you looking for?

542
00:34:11,585 --> 00:34:13,570
Is Ran at home?

543
00:34:13,570 --> 00:34:15,200
Don't call her.

544
00:34:15,200 --> 00:34:16,560
Ran?

545
00:34:18,130 --> 00:34:20,955
Isn't this Mr. Chaisak's house?

546
00:34:20,955 --> 00:34:22,460
Chaisak...

547
00:34:22,460 --> 00:34:24,645
Oh, the previous owner

548
00:34:24,645 --> 00:34:26,520
I bought this house from?

549
00:34:26,520 --> 00:34:28,093
He sold this house?

550
00:34:28,093 --> 00:34:31,078
Do you know where he moved to?

551
00:34:31,078 --> 00:34:33,593
Well, after Chaisak passed away,

552
00:34:33,593 --> 00:34:35,818
his wife couldn't afford the mortgage.

553
00:34:35,818 --> 00:34:37,363
So she sold it

554
00:34:37,363 --> 00:34:40,468
and moved away with her kids.

555
00:34:40,468 --> 00:34:43,188
But she didn't mention where she went.

556
00:34:57,840 --> 00:35:01,440
We have to meet with Mr. Luknut's agency now.

557
00:35:04,703 --> 00:35:06,560
Do you think...

558
00:35:07,921 --> 00:35:10,631
it's idiotic to believe that kid?

559
00:35:10,631 --> 00:35:14,160
I trust your intuition.

560
00:35:14,160 --> 00:35:17,345
Don't tell anyone that I came here,

561
00:35:17,345 --> 00:35:19,465
or what we're about to do.

562
00:35:20,793 --> 00:35:22,320
Especially...

563
00:35:22,320 --> 00:35:24,120
you know who.

564
00:35:28,579 --> 00:35:30,499
Yes, Mrs. Angkhana?

565
00:35:33,713 --> 00:35:34,931
Yes.

566
00:35:34,931 --> 00:35:36,851
Who are you meeting with?

567
00:35:38,035 --> 00:35:40,675
An event organizer

568
00:35:41,880 --> 00:35:44,705
for the new TV series lineup reveal?

569
00:35:44,705 --> 00:35:46,810
Which company is it?

570
00:35:46,810 --> 00:35:49,475
Oh, Sonix Youth?

571
00:35:49,475 --> 00:35:51,340
The one owned by Kong Piya?

572
00:35:51,340 --> 00:35:53,480
Yeah.

573
00:35:53,480 --> 00:35:56,080
Yeah, yeah, that's all.

574
00:35:59,828 --> 00:36:04,653
He's been out since those
fans caused a scene out front.

575
00:36:04,653 --> 00:36:05,758
I think...

576
00:36:05,758 --> 00:36:07,800
Yai couldn't have met that woman.

577
00:36:07,800 --> 00:36:10,705
How can you be so sure?

578
00:36:10,705 --> 00:36:14,480
Then can you help me look into the reason

579
00:36:14,480 --> 00:36:15,985
why she came here

580
00:36:15,985 --> 00:36:17,770
and what her purpose is?

581
00:36:17,770 --> 00:36:19,120
Nana,

582
00:36:19,120 --> 00:36:24,760
don't let that woman bring your mood down.

583
00:36:24,760 --> 00:36:27,360
Whatever the reason she's here
or whoever she came with.

584
00:36:27,360 --> 00:36:29,985
Even if she came to see Yai,

585
00:36:29,985 --> 00:36:33,644
he would still never go back
and choose her again.

586
00:36:33,644 --> 00:36:36,160
"Yai would never choose her",

587
00:36:36,160 --> 00:36:39,080
but does that mean he would choose me?

588
00:36:41,040 --> 00:36:42,241
Well...

589
00:36:43,040 --> 00:36:44,960
of course.

590
00:36:48,160 --> 00:36:50,425
If Yai had chosen me,

591
00:36:50,425 --> 00:36:54,185
I'd already be married with kids, Auntie.

592
00:37:04,575 --> 00:37:06,160
Why do you have to be so angry?

593
00:37:06,160 --> 00:37:09,200
I already told you I did my duty as a fan!

594
00:37:09,200 --> 00:37:11,825
Because what you did
could've landed you in jail.

595
00:37:11,825 --> 00:37:13,810
It's a good thing they didn't arrest you.

596
00:37:13,810 --> 00:37:16,235
Otherwise, your future would be
ruined by a criminal record.

597
00:37:16,235 --> 00:37:18,040
Don't go there again.

598
00:37:18,040 --> 00:37:20,120
Can't I even go there to see Sam for a bit?

599
00:37:20,120 --> 00:37:23,265
You already saw how nice he was to his fans.

600
00:37:23,265 --> 00:37:25,840
- No!
- No!

601
00:37:25,840 --> 00:37:28,600
Okay, okay, fine.

602
00:37:28,600 --> 00:37:29,800
Go to your room.

603
00:37:29,800 --> 00:37:32,505
You're grounded for two days.

604
00:37:32,505 --> 00:37:34,480
Ran!

605
00:37:34,480 --> 00:37:35,920
Dao.

606
00:37:42,840 --> 00:37:44,200
Hello.

607
00:37:45,659 --> 00:37:47,040
Oh.

608
00:37:47,040 --> 00:37:48,680
You're the security guard.

609
00:37:50,200 --> 00:37:51,920
What job again?

610
00:37:55,243 --> 00:37:57,508
No, I'm not interested.

611
00:37:57,508 --> 00:37:59,268
Thank you for calling me.

612
00:38:00,681 --> 00:38:02,971
Ran... What was the job?

613
00:38:02,971 --> 00:38:04,760
Why didn't you take it?

614
00:38:04,760 --> 00:38:06,920
You still haven't found a job, have you?

615
00:38:08,674 --> 00:38:12,354
It's a job at MJTV station, where "he" is.

616
00:38:14,360 --> 00:38:16,520
I'll soak the soy beans, Mom.

617
00:38:45,120 --> 00:38:47,440
[2026]

618
00:38:47,440 --> 00:38:49,720
[2013]

619
00:39:11,520 --> 00:39:13,360
Hey, pass it to me.

620
00:39:18,003 --> 00:39:20,628
Who are you passing it to? I'm right here.

621
00:39:20,628 --> 00:39:23,040
This person is my girlfriend.

622
00:39:23,040 --> 00:39:26,160
Wow!

623
00:39:26,160 --> 00:39:27,800
- Hey!
- For real?

624
00:39:27,800 --> 00:39:30,320
- Since when have you two been dating?
- Since now.

625
00:39:30,320 --> 00:39:31,920
Wow!

626
00:39:31,920 --> 00:39:34,000
Ran!

627
00:39:34,000 --> 00:39:35,800
Did I hear it right?

628
00:39:41,064 --> 00:39:43,268
Ran... stop!

629
00:39:43,268 --> 00:39:45,400
Hey, why are you blushing?

630
00:39:45,400 --> 00:39:47,225
Does this mean you're really dating Yai?

631
00:39:47,225 --> 00:39:50,290
Hey, keep your voice down.

632
00:39:50,290 --> 00:39:53,291
Really? Well, if it's Yai, I approve.

633
00:39:53,291 --> 00:39:56,840
He's smart, athletic, and rich, too.

634
00:39:56,840 --> 00:40:00,225
If I hadn't been your wingman that day...

635
00:40:00,225 --> 00:40:01,800
When?

636
00:40:01,800 --> 00:40:04,560
The day you saw those two juniors making out.

637
00:40:06,000 --> 00:40:09,414
So you two are officially dating now?

638
00:40:09,414 --> 00:40:10,880
Tell me, please, please.

639
00:40:10,880 --> 00:40:12,000
Nooch.

640
00:40:12,000 --> 00:40:15,720
- Right?
- Don't know. Don't care.

641
00:40:15,720 --> 00:40:16,800
Let me tell you

642
00:40:16,800 --> 00:40:19,280
I was the one who told him
you went upstairs alone.

643
00:40:19,280 --> 00:40:24,080
The moment he heard that, he bolted after you.

644
00:40:24,080 --> 00:40:25,400
Ran!

645
00:40:25,400 --> 00:40:26,720
Tell me first.

646
00:40:26,720 --> 00:40:28,960
Are you two dating now?

647
00:40:31,360 --> 00:40:32,720
Yai.

648
00:40:34,400 --> 00:40:35,920
Why did you have to steal her from me?

649
00:40:35,920 --> 00:40:37,680
You already have Nana, don't you?

650
00:40:37,680 --> 00:40:39,160
Why steal her from me too?

651
00:40:39,160 --> 00:40:41,360
I don't have feelings for Nana at all.

652
00:40:41,360 --> 00:40:42,720
I'll let it slide since it's you.

653
00:40:42,720 --> 00:40:44,276
If it were anyone else, I wouldn't allow it.

654
00:40:44,276 --> 00:40:45,756
Yai.

655
00:40:47,825 --> 00:40:51,730
I heard... you're dating Daran?

656
00:40:53,560 --> 00:40:56,160
What about me?

657
00:40:56,160 --> 00:40:57,865
What do you mean?

658
00:40:57,865 --> 00:40:59,960
You know what I mean.

659
00:40:59,960 --> 00:41:01,400
Stop joking around.

660
00:41:01,400 --> 00:41:03,280
I'm being serious.

661
00:41:05,080 --> 00:41:06,320
Okay.

662
00:41:06,320 --> 00:41:08,353
I'll be serious.

663
00:41:08,353 --> 00:41:12,040
I don't like you the way you like me.

664
00:41:12,040 --> 00:41:13,800
I like Daran,

665
00:41:13,800 --> 00:41:15,840
and she has to be my girlfriend.

666
00:41:16,986 --> 00:41:18,386
Is that clear?

667
00:41:19,508 --> 00:41:20,948
Yai.

668
00:41:24,560 --> 00:41:25,720
Hey, hey, hey.

669
00:41:25,720 --> 00:41:27,240
Hey!

670
00:41:30,040 --> 00:41:31,320
Me again?

671
00:42:07,880 --> 00:42:09,880
Mom, I'll...

672
00:42:13,090 --> 00:42:14,531
Mom!

673
00:42:15,355 --> 00:42:16,789
Mom!

674
00:42:17,811 --> 00:42:19,251
Mom.

675
00:42:20,920 --> 00:42:22,195
Mom.

676
00:42:27,015 --> 00:42:28,560
<i>How do I convince you, then?</i>

677
00:42:28,560 --> 00:42:31,501
<i>Marry Nana, and I'll believe you!</i>

678
00:42:31,501 --> 00:42:33,400
<i>You two were apart for more than ten years,</i>

679
00:42:33,400 --> 00:42:35,040
<i>then suddenly met again.</i>

680
00:42:35,040 --> 00:42:36,880
<i>It must have happened for a reason.</i>

681
00:42:36,880 --> 00:42:39,860
<i>I'll just keep being a thorn in your side</i>

682
00:42:39,860 --> 00:42:41,899
<i>until you finally give up.</i>

683
00:42:41,899 --> 00:42:43,160
<i>Is that Mr. Alex's girlfriend?</i>

684
00:42:43,160 --> 00:42:44,200
<i>He gets so close to her.</i>

685
00:42:44,200 --> 00:42:46,120
<i>He has never done this to anyone.</i>

686
00:42:46,120 --> 00:42:48,008
<i>What will you do if you meet him?</i>

687
00:42:48,008 --> 00:42:49,480
<i>It can't be helped.</i>

688
00:42:49,480 --> 00:42:52,800
<i>I'll just fulfill my duty as best as I can.</i>
